b.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm not sure this note is necessary. I understand the frustration, but... I personally see little ambiguity or confusion over this. Nowhere it is implied that the scene tree would unpause itself when calling `change_scene_to_file` & co., nor it is exhaustive, as the current scene can be also changed with a corresponding property.\nThe note is also way too long for basically saying \"_This property is unaffected when the scene is changed_\" which, I reiterate, I believe there's little confusion for.\n\nInstead of adding a note, if there's something in the documentation, or any other aspect of the engine, that made you believe in this behavior, that's what should be addressed.\n\n... Could it be the wording of `change_scene_to_file()` and similar? Had I written this description, I would've not said the following:\n> Changes the running scene to the one at the given [param path]\n\nPerhaps the confusion stems from \"the **running** scene\", as it may imply the scene \"begins running again\" as soon as it is changed. It should've just said \"the current scene\", because that's what it is.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119743#pullrequestreview-4357938870","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119743","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119743#pullrequestreview-4357938870"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119743"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-25T16:53:13Z","commit_id":"ce4dbcdd340961c9e1ce266a34fa64baca9a6925"}]